# shellcheck shell=bash
# shellcheck disable=SC2034  # read by the pipeline stages that source it
# Site settings for the pipeline.
#
# Copy this file to `cluster.conf` in the same folder and fill it in:
#
#     cp cluster.conf.example cluster.conf
#
# `cluster.conf` is ignored by git and must never be committed. It is the
# one place where storage paths and other site values live. A stage reads
# it with `lab_load_cluster_conf` (pipeline/lib/common.sh) and names the
# values it needs; a missing file, a syntax error, or a value that is
# unset, empty, or still CHANGE_ME stops the stage with a message. To read
# a file at another path, set LAB_CLUSTER_CONF to it.

# --- SLURM identity ---------------------------------------------------
# No job script carries `#SBATCH --account=` or `--mail-user=`, and no
# stage passes either. Export SBATCH_ACCOUNT in your shell profile on the
# cluster; sbatch reads it as the default account. With no --mail-user,
# SLURM notifies the submitting user.
#
# Not read by any stage. Kept for one case: if that mail does not arrive,
# a submit wrapper may pass this address as --mail-user.
# SLURM_MAIL_USER=""

# --- Storage ----------------------------------------------------------
# Where the simulations run and where finished data is kept.
SCRATCH_DIR="${HOME}/scratch"
PROJECT_DIR="${HOME}/CHANGE_ME"

# --- Software ---------------------------------------------------------
# The Python environment that has `polyphys_lab` installed. Leave empty
# to use what is already active. The modules a LAMMPS run loads are its
# variant's MODULES, in study.conf.
LAB_PYTHON_ENV=""

# --- This repository --------------------------------------------------
# Where polyphys-lab is cloned on the cluster. A study kept in another
# repository finds the stages of pipeline/ through it.
LAB_DIR="${HOME}/polyphys-lab"
